// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3570004205" "So you're {Villainname}.  I've heard about you.  Not all good things, I assure you.  I suppose you want to know about Inventions.  Everydone does.  Inventions inventions inventions.  Don't you guys have Heroes to harass?  Sheesh.<br><br>You're still here.  FINE.  I'll tell you about Inventions, hope it's not too complicated for you.  You're probably not as smart as I am.  I am pretty brilliant, you know.  But since you've made it this far, I SUPPOSE you'll be able to muddle your way through.<br><br>Let me dumb it down for you.  Have you noticed that junk that you've been picking up along the way? I would hope so, considering it's been six levels.<br><br>There are two kinds of salvage: Base Salvage and Invention Salvage. Base salvage is used to create items for your Supergroups' base, and can be used for your advantage during base raids.  Invention Salvage is something you can use to craft enhancements, so you can use these enhancements on your character or auction them away.  Your choice, I don't care.<br><br>There are two types of Invention Salvage dropped: Tech and Magic. These two types will determine what you will be able to invent. I'm way too important to spend my time explaining more to you, so go see Dr. Gillett across the way and he'll tell you more about crafting.  Go!<br><br><color deepskyblue>There are two types of salvage dropped by enemies when defeated: Base Salvage and Invention Salvage. Base Salvage is used to create items for your Supergroups' base; whereas, Invention Salvage is used to create enhancements for yourself.  You can buy and sell Invention Salvage and Recipes at the Black Market in Mercy Island, Sharkhead Isle, and St. Martial.  The two types of Invention Salvage that are dropped are Magic and Technology.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P3992470203" "Get more information from Dr. Gillett."
// SendOffString :
"P2699672969" "Kevin will give you some more information about the invention system.  I'm too important to waste any more of my time explaining this to you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - V_SL2.5_Inv_Tutorial_Compound1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2513532475" "Talk to Dr. Kevin Gillett"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2721678839" "Why are you wasting my time?  Go see Dr. Gillett.  You want information, he's your guy.  Sheesh.  You're blocking me now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3247700781" "Hello there, {VillainName}.  Dr. Yu sent you over.  You have that flushed frustrated look about you.  Don't mind him.  All bluster no substance.  So, anyway, I have some more information about the invention salvage you've been collecting. It's a good thing that you've reached level ten, or trying to craft or slot enhancements would be a waste of time since you cannot craft until you reach this level.  There are three different types of invention salvage that drop: Common, Uncommon and Rare. Common salvage is used with the recipes that are found at the universities and your Supergroups' base crafting tables (if you have one).  Samuel O'Reilly will tell you more about the Uncommon and Rare invention salvage later on.<br><br>Oh!  Since I am helping you, please do me a big favor!  Freedom Corps have broken into our storage facility and are stealing salvage. Get in there and stop them before they get any more of our supplies!<br><br><color deepskyblue> Invention salvage dropped will have three different types rarity: Common, Uncommon and Rare. The Common salvage can be used with the invention tables in the universities and, if your Supergroup's base has one, your invention table.</color><br><br> Stop the Arachnos looters before they steal all the salvage!"

