"P3797354409" "You really should go see Charles Ball inside the university.  He'll help you use that salvage you have. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2258924925" "Hi there.  Charles said you'd be coming by.  He told me you wanted to learn how to make invented enhancements.  Easy enough.  Let's go through it, shall we?  The first thing you're going to do is go to the invention table and touch it.<br><img src=COV_Inv_Table.tga> <br><br>The invention tables will show you all the Common enhancements that you can make.  It takes a mere fraction of Infamy to create.  Look here.  See how the enhancements will identify their functions in their title?  Very handy!<br><img src=COV_Inv_UI.tga><br><br>Why don't you go ahead and play around to see what you can make.  Oh and be sure that you have to have room in your inventory for the enhancement, or it won't let you create one.  Also, bear in mind that the maximum craft enhancement level you can create is three levels higher than your current level.<br><img src=COV_Inv_Arrow.tga><br><br>When you decide what enhancement to make, go ahead and then talk to Samuel O'Reilly.  I've alerted him that you'll be dropping by and he's waiting to tell you more about these invented enhancements.<br><br>Oh.  Heh.  Heh.  I almost forgot.  If your Supergroup has a base with a workshop room and a crafting table, you have the ability to create enhancements outside of the university. The process is the same, and instead of having to be in a certain zone, you can go to your base at any time and make these invented enhancements using the crafing table and your invention salvage.  <color deepskyblue>Touch the invention table<br><img src=COV_Inv_Table.tga> to make an enhancement.<br><img src=COV_Inv_UI.tga><br><br>Take note of the different kinds of enhancements that you can create and what they do.<br><img src=COH_Inv_Arrow.tga><br><br>Make sure that there is room in your enhancement tray, or it won't let you invent the enhancement.<br></color>"

