// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1789408967" "Talk to Samuel O'Reilly "
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4074380717" "Mr. O'Reilly will help you complete your training in invention crafting.  Do go see him."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3374072897" "Charles showed you the invention tables?  Right.  Good.  Excellent.  Now here are some facts you don't want to forget while you are inventing these enhancements.<br><br>The strength of the invented enhancement won't change. Don't worry about out-leveling your slotted enhancement because it will always give you the bonus it was created at. You can always slot your enhancement up to three levels higher than your current level, but you will not get any more of a bonus that you normally would.<br><br>Not only are recipes available at the universities and crafting tables, but enemies can drop recipes along with invention salvage.  These recipes can be used with all your salvage for better inventions and costume pieces.  eep an eye out for these, because, like Inspirations, they can only be used once and then will disappear. <br><br>Go chat with Dr. Bright.  He can tell you about some special enhancement sets and what they can do for you.  I almost forgot.  Your Origin is completely irrelevant when creating these enhancements.  How wonderful!<br><br>The uncommon and rare enhancements can also use recipes that are dropped by enemies that you defeat along the way. These recipes will help you invent better enhancements than the invention tables can offer. You can view your different recipes in the recipe tab located in the salvage window.<br><img src=COV_Inv_Inventory.tga><br><br><color deepskyblue>The invented enhancements are level based, and you will never outgrow your created enhancement. You can invent enhancements up to a maximum of three levels higher than your current level. Also, your Origin is completely irrelevant. The Uncommon and Rare enhancements can also use recipes that are dropped by enemies that you defeat along the way.  These recipes will help you invent better enhancements than the invention tables can offer.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - V_SL2.5_Inv_Tutorial_Compound1_Part7 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4156368752" "Talk to Dr. Bright"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1235760225" "Dr. James Bright will help you complete your training in invention crafting."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1971826314" "So Samuel let you know about the special enhancement sets that can be created?  Excellent.  Let me tell you a little more about these very useful sets, called Powersets. There are some enhancements that work together within a power to give you special bonuses.  The more you have, the better the bonus. A nice thing about Uncommon and Rare crafted enhancements is that even though the effect is lower than a Common crafted enhancement, they have multiple results. Let's take a look at the Bonesnap set for example. <br><img src=COV_Inv_Bonesnap.tga><br><br>Uncommon and Rare enhancements are used in these special powersets.  When slotting these special crafted enhancements, you will gain multiple permanent benefits.  A Powerset can use as little as three enhancements up to all six, but can only be slotted with other enhancements of the same set.  These specific sets do have level and power limitations.<br><br>The set bonuses will give you a powerful advantage when used efficiently.  When these enhancement sets are slotted in the same power, they create a bonus that will always be active.  You can have as many enhancement sets as you have available powers.  Also, as soon as you slot these enhancements the advantage is overall, not just for the power that the crafted enhancement is located in.<br><img src=COV_Inv_Bone_Slot.tga><br><br><color deepskyblue>The Uncommon and Rare crafted enhancements slot into Powersets, which give you multiple permanent benefits.  When these enhancement sets are slotted in the same power, they create a bonus that affects your overall character, not just that specific power. You can have as many enhancement sets as you have available powers.  You do not have to have the power activated to receive the bonus.</color>"

